cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "G_CAPSUL / CAPSULE: a retained assembly for unified lossless FASTQ compression, reference-free variant calling, and reference-free locus retrieval"
authors:
  - family-names: "Balashanmugam"
    given-names: "Thackshanaramana"
version: 1.1.1
date-released: "2026-09-26"
url: "https://github.com/thackshanaramana0-spec/g_capsul"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thackshanaramana0-spec/g_capsul"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - FASTQ compression
  - reference-free variant calling
  - genome assembly
  - pseudogenome
  - bioinformatics
abstract: >-
  A lossless FASTQ archive that also supports reference-free variant calling
  and reference-free locus retrieval, all from a single retained
  representation with no external reference genome or external tool at
  runtime. 19/19 datasets smaller than SPRING, 19/19 smaller than Genozip,
  57/57 archives verified lossless. Het-SNV calling from the archive alone
  reaches mean F1 0.876 across four GIAB individuals. Reference-free locus
  retrieval recovers both allelic read sets at 1,452 of 1,452 heterozygous
  sites across four individuals and two loci.
